SUMMARY:Deadline: Loeb Fellowship 2027-28 at Harvard Graduate School of Des
 ign
DESCRIPTION:The Loeb Fellowship at Harvard Graduate School of Design is a y
 ear-long residential fellowship for accomplished mid-career practitioners 
 shaping the built and natural environment: urban designers\, public artist
 s\, architects\, landscape architects\, urban planners\, developers\, jour
 nalists\, civic leaders\, policymakers and community development leaders (
 past fellows have included a theater director\, public artists and a docum
 entary filmmaker). Fellows audit courses at the GSD and across Harvard (mi
 nimum one GSD course per semester)\, engage with the school community\, an
 d join a lifelong global alumni network. SUPPORT: a stipend of USD 57\,500
  for the academic year (taxable income)\, housing through 30 June for fell
 ows and families of modest size coming from outside the Boston/Cambridge a
 rea\, and a travel grant covering roughly one economy round trip home per 
 semester. ELIGIBILITY: minimum 8 years of experience in the field (a typic
 al class averages about 42 years of age)\; international candidates are en
 couraged to apply and must be eligible for a J-1 visa at selection\; fello
 ws must remain in residence in the Cambridge area while classes are in ses
 sion. HOW TO APPLY: via SlideRoom with a resume\, three recommendation let
 ters (due 7 days after the deadline) and optional supplemental materials. 
 No application fee. DEADLINE: 5 January 2027 at 11:59 PM ET for the 2027-2
 8 class.\n\nOrganisation: Harvard Graduate School of Design\nLocation: Har
 vard Graduate School of Design\, Cambridge\, Massachusetts\, US. Open inte
 rnationally\; fellows must remain in residence in the Cambridge area while
  classes are in session (J-1 visa for international fellows).\nAward: Stip
 end of USD 57\,500 for the academic year (taxable)\, plus housing for fell
 ows and their families coming from outside the Boston/Cambridge area throu
 gh 30 June\, and a travel grant covering approximately one economy round t
 rip home per semester. No application fee.\nDuration: One academic year in
  residence\, through 30 June\n\nMore: https://loebfellowship.gsd.harvard.e
 du/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://loebfellowship.gsd.harvard.edu/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugra
 ntdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Harvard Graduate School of Design\, Cambridge\, Massachusetts\, US
 . Open internationally\; fellows must remain in residence in the Cambridge
  area while classes are in session (J-1 visa for international fellows).
END:VEVENT
