SUMMARY:Deadline: CISAC (Stanford): Fellowships 2027-2028 (AI\, Nuclear & I
 nternational Security)
DESCRIPTION:CISAC's 2027-2028 fellowship application is open across seven t
 racks: Artificial Intelligence and Laws of Armed Conflict\; AI in Strategi
 c Stability and Military Competition\; Geopolitics of Artificial Intellige
 nce\; India-U.S. Security Studies\; Natural Sciences or Engineering Intern
 ational Security (for natural scientists and engineers researching scienti
 fic and technical aspects of security topics)\; Nuclear Security\; and Int
 ernational Security. Applicants are considered for all fellowships they ar
 e eligible for. Fellows spend the academic year in residence at Stanford e
 ngaged in research and writing\, participating in seminars and collaborati
 ng with CISAC faculty and the wider community. CAREER STAGES: predoctoral 
 (currently enrolled PhD students)\, postdoctoral (completed PhD or DPhil)\
 , and junior faculty or professionals. FUNDING: stipends are provided (pre
 doctoral comparable to Stanford Graduate Fellowships plus tuition\; postdo
 ctoral and professional stipends commensurate with experience)\, though ex
 act amounts are not published\; non-US citizens may apply and visas are av
 ailable through the fellowship. APPLY via the SlideRoom portal (Stanford C
 ISAC Fellowship Program) with the application form\, CV\, graduate transcr
 ipt (required for pre- and postdoctoral applicants)\, research prospectus 
 (max 1\,500 words)\, abstract (max 200 words)\, writing sample (max 50 pag
 es)\, and three confidential recommendation letters uploaded directly by r
 ecommenders\; all materials in English. DEADLINE: 2 December 2026. Questio
 ns: cisacfellowship@stanford.edu.\n\nOrganisation: Center for Internationa
 l Security and Cooperation (CISAC)\, Stanford FSI\nLocation: Stanford\, Ca
 lifornia\, USA (in-residence\; fellows are expected to be fully present an
 d engaged at CISAC)\nAward: Funded in-residence fellowship. Predoctoral fe
 llows receive stipends comparable to the Stanford Graduate Fellowships pro
 gram\, plus CISAC pays non-matriculated student tuition\; postdoctoral and
  junior-faculty/professional fellows receive stipends commensurate with ex
 perience and Stanford's established minimums. Specific dollar figures are 
 not published. No application fee.\nDuration: 2027-2028 academic year in r
 esidence at Stanford\n\nMore: https://cisac.fsi.stanford.edu/content/cisac
 -fellowships?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://cisac.fsi.stanford.edu/content/cisac-fellowships?utm_source=art
 ificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Stanford\, California\, USA (in-residence\; fellows are expected t
 o be fully present and engaged at CISAC)
END:VEVENT
